---@class aws.redshift_data.ListTablesRequest
---@field ClusterIdentifier? aws.redshift_data.ClusterIdentifierString The cluster identifier. This parameter is required when connecting to a cluster and authenticating using either Secrets Manager or temporary credentials.
---@field SecretArn? aws.redshift_data.SecretArn The name or ARN of the secret that enables access to the database. This parameter is required when authenticating using Secrets Manager.
---@field DbUser? aws.redshift_data.String The database user name. This parameter is required when connecting to a cluster as a database user and authenticating using temporary credentials.
---@field Database aws.redshift_data.String The name of the database that contains the tables to list. If ConnectedDatabase is not specified, this is also the database to connect to with your authentication credentials.
---@field ConnectedDatabase? aws.redshift_data.String A database name. The connected database is specified when you connect with your authentication credentials.
---@field SchemaPattern? aws.redshift_data.String A pattern to filter results by schema name. Within a schema pattern, "%" means match any substring of 0 or more characters and "_" means match any one character. Only schema name entries matching the search pattern are returned. If SchemaPattern is not specified, then all tables that match TablePattern are returned. If neither SchemaPattern or TablePattern are specified, then all tables are return...
---@field TablePattern? aws.redshift_data.String A pattern to filter results by table name. Within a table pattern, "%" means match any substring of 0 or more characters and "_" means match any one character. Only table name entries matching the search pattern are returned. If TablePattern is not specified, then all tables that match SchemaPatternare returned. If neither SchemaPattern or TablePattern are specified, then all tables are returned.
---@field NextToken? aws.redshift_data.String A value that indicates the starting point for the next set of response records in a subsequent request. If a value is returned in a response, you can retrieve the next set of records by providing this returned NextToken value in the next NextToken parameter and retrying the command. If the NextToken field is empty, all response records have been retrieved for the request.
---@field MaxResults? aws.redshift_data.PageSize The maximum number of tables to return in the response. If more tables exist than fit in one response, then NextToken is returned to page through the results.
---@field WorkgroupName? aws.redshift_data.WorkgroupNameString The serverless workgroup name or Amazon Resource Name (ARN). This parameter is required when connecting to a serverless workgroup and authenticating using either Secrets Manager or temporary credentials.

